{
	"source": "docs/official/Pokemon Locations.xlsx, sheet 'Unavailable Pokemon' (the R&B author's own workbook)",
	"provenance": "transcribed",
	"purpose": [
		"Which species this hack REMOVED. Without it the tool has one word for two",
		"opposite situations: ask.js where Kubfu and ask.js where Caterpie both",
		"answered NOT FINDABLE, though one is a guaranteed free gift and the other",
		"can never be obtained. For a nuzlocke those are the two most different",
		"answers there are."
	],
	"reconciliation": [
		"Cross-checked every named species against the ROM-derived wild tables.",
		"8 of 416 appear in both, which is a contradiction that had to be explained",
		"rather than silently resolved.",
		"",
		"SIX are explained: their only wild source is content the R&B tracker never",
		"lists and availability.json therefore cannot date — Safari Zone Southeast",
		"and Northeast, and Artisan Cave. Unreachable content still carries its ROM",
		"tables. Those six are genuinely unavailable and the two sources agree once",
		"reachability is accounted for.",
		"",
		"TWO are a real disagreement and are NOT claimed either way below. Geodude",
		"sits in Magma Hideout 3F room 2, and Duraludon across four Shoal Cave rooms",
		"dated 1178 — both reachable by our own data. Either the workbook is stale",
		"for them, or the tool is missing a gate those rooms sit behind (Shoal Cave",
		"has tide state this model does not carry). Recorded as an open question."
	],
	"openQuestions": [
		{
			"species": "Geodude",
			"wildSource": "MAP_MAGMA_HIDEOUT_3F_2R walk L27",
			"question": "The workbook calls Geodude unavailable but this room is reachable. Is the room actually enterable?"
		},
		{
			"species": "Duraludon",
			"wildSource": "4 Shoal Cave low-tide rooms, walk L72, dated 1178",
			"question": "The workbook calls Duraludon unavailable but Shoal Cave is dated and reachable. Does low tide gate it in a way the model does not carry?"
		}
	],
